From 63f907541d8037309395f675f83d488581cc7a79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kunstbanause <3209654+Kunstbanause@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:26:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] d/rift_s, t/constellation: Refine tracked priors, drop stale
 fixes, gyro-checked resets

Measured with the tracking protocol (ctrl-protocol.py / ctrl-analyze.py),
WayVR only, no CPU load: no dropped camera frames, yet 25-30 dropouts per
minute and 12-18 % wrong matches during slow smooth motion, and the left
controller's filter reset itself 84 times in 5 minutes, mostly onto fixes
30-180 degrees off the gyro orientation.

Constellation tracker:
- The fast path only accepted the prior pose as is: projected LEDs had
  to land within the LED's own radius (~1.7 px at 40 cm), but a tracked
  prior is typically 5 mm off (2-3 px). It failed for half the frames in
  smooth motion and ~90 % in fast motion, leaving the broad searches,
  which produce the wrong matches. New path for tracked priors: pair
  blobs with the projected LEDs as mutual nearest neighbours within 6 px,
  RANSAC-PnP from the prior, accept only if it still agrees with the
  prior (T_CONSTELLATION_POSE_FROM_PRIOR_REFINED).
- When the RANSAC refinement in submit_device_pose() failed, the
  unrefined prior or last seen pose was submitted as an observation:
  the device's own prediction, or an old pose (~10 % of fixes, identical
  consecutive positions). Drop those instead.
- CONSTELLATION_PRIOR_REFINE=0 restores the old behaviour for A/B tests.

Rift S controller:
- The tracker prior fallback (filter not tracking: 3DoF orientation plus
  last optical position) no longer claims POSITION_TRACKED, so the tracker
  only refines priors the filter actually tracks.
- Fusion: while the orientation is trusted (accepted fix within
  reset_trust_time = 2 s), consistency and forced resets only go to fixes
  within reset_rot_max = 20 degrees of the filter. Wrong LED matches are
  often consistent with each other (a flipped ring) but far off the gyro.
  After the trust time the old rules apply, so a wrong state can't lock
  in. Replayed on the recording: resets e.g. 11 -> 1 (hands close) and
  22 -> 10 (watch gesture); with 1 s trust a wrong pose came back (tilt
  error at rest p90 37 deg), with 2 s it stays correct.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
